SUPPLEMENT 1 — EXACT CANONICAL CLARIFICATIONS

1. MARKET-CONDITIONING ESTIMATOR

For:

RET_MOM × MARKET_SPY_TREND10 — POSITIVE — 7d
RET_MOM × MARKET_SPY_TREND10 — POSITIVE — 10d

preserve the upstream B4 two-stage estimator.

Stage 1, for every eligible trading date t:

cross-sectional regression:

forward_return_i,t,h

a_t,h + b_t,h * RET_MOM_rank_i,t + error_i,t,h

Extract b_t,h.

Stage 2:

b_t,h

alpha_h + gamma_h * Z_t + u_t,h

where Z_t is the frozen causally standardized SPY TREND10 market state.

The PRIMARY scientific estimand is:

gamma_h

the Stage-2 coefficient on market state.

Primary inference on gamma_h uses Bartlett/Newey-West HAC with:

lag = horizon - 1 trading dates.

Material standardized effect:

ES_h = gamma_h / sample_SD(b_t,h)

using ddof=1.

Material threshold:

abs(ES_h) >= 0.20

The mean, median, SD and sign share of b_t,h are diagnostic statistics only. They are not substitutes for gamma_h.

For temporal robustness, refit the COMPLETE two-stage estimator independently inside each prospectively fixed chronological block.

For leave-top-five/symbol-concentration robustness, remove the specified symbols from Stage 1 and recompute the complete Stage-1 -> Stage-2 estimator.

Do not use the previously rejected same-date four-column interaction regression.

2. MECHANICAL DISPOSITION TRUTH TABLE

Every registered B5 hypothesis receives exactly one disposition.

NOT_TESTABLE

Use only when the primary scientific estimand cannot validly be computed because of semantic, data or numerical insufficiency.

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_SUPPORTED

Requires ALL of:

* frozen hypothesized direction passes;
* abs(standardized effect) >= 0.20;
* BH-adjusted q <= 0.05;
* every required robustness gate passes;
* no semantic/data-integrity failure.

PARTIAL_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE

Use when:

* frozen hypothesized direction passes;
* abs(standardized effect) >= 0.20;
* BH-adjusted q <= 0.05;

BUT one or more required robustness gates fails.

INDEPENDENT_VALIDATION_FAILED

Use when any primary confirmation requirement fails:

* hypothesized direction;
* material-effect threshold; OR
* BH-FDR requirement.

A zero primary effect FAILS the directional gate.

Missing/unavailable required robustness diagnostics fail SUPPORT but do not convert an otherwise validly computable primary estimand into NOT_TESTABLE.

LIMITED_TEMPORAL_CAPACITY remains an independent flag and never changes the mechanical disposition.

3. ADJACENT-HORIZON COHERENCE

Retain the upstream adjacent-horizon robustness concept using the frozen horizon grid:

1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 10 trading days.

However, apply adjacency ONLY when the adjacent horizon is itself an already registered B5 primary case in the same factor family.

Do NOT compute an unregistered horizon merely to create an adjacent comparison.

An absent grid neighbor:

* is not a failure;
* does not create an unavailable diagnostic;
* does not authorize another scientific test.

Preserve the registered nine-case family exactly.

For applicable registered adjacent cases, evaluate the inherited coherence requirement prospectively and report it as a robustness gate.

4. OTHER INHERITED ROBUSTNESS RULES

Retain:

* temporal directional support in at least 3 of 4 prospectively fixed chronological blocks;
* no single block contributes more than 50% of absolute aggregate effect;
* leave-top-five removal must not reverse the aggregate primary-effect sign;
* zero after leave-top-five removal is not a sign reversal;
* unavailable required robustness diagnostics fail support.

The B5 case-specific four chronological blocks supersede earlier B4 full-panel blocks for B5 validation.

5. SCOPE OF SUPERSESSION

Supplement 1 changes or clarifies ONLY:

* market-conditioning primary estimator/estimand;
* disposition truth table;
* registered-case-only adjacent-horizon coherence.

All other provisions of:

SW10_S2_B5_VALIDATION_PROTOCOL_V1

remain frozen and controlling.

